<!--
  Speech Studio's Swift sidecar runs MLX-Swift statically linked (verified by
  inspecting Speech Studio.app/Contents — only two Mach-O binaries, no
  embedded dylibs or frameworks). Metal is loaded from the system framework
  path so library validation always accepts it. The sidecar opens no audio
  input, no network sockets the sandbox would care about, and reads/writes
  user-owned cache dirs that hardened runtime does not gate.

  Result: minimum-privilege under hardened runtime is an empty entitlement
  set. The re-sign step in CI applies this to override the app-wide
  entitlements (mic, JIT) that Tauri's bundler stamps onto the sidecar by
  default — those are irrelevant to the sidecar and removing them shrinks
  attack surface on the most privileged process (it holds the loaded TTS
  model).

  Re-add entries here only with a concrete crash log or load failure
  reproducing the need.
-->
